{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgbxUj4TwiV1oiQafaiF4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AbYkmGFpPM41o7qnFxkRzv","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"kill 1305; cd /work && ./board post run_report '{\"status\": \"failed\", \"task\": \"self_diffusion of liquid Li at 800 K (thermostat equilibration, then NVE velocity-Verlet production with energy-drift check)\", \"reason\": \"Premise is fine: Li melts at 453.7 K, so 800 K is well inside the liquid range, and D is measurable by MSD in ps-scale NVE MD. The run did not finish within the compute and budget available. Setup: ASE 3.29 + MACE-MP-0 medium (mace-torch 0.3.15), dt 1 fs. Melt at 1500 K (Langevin), then NPTBerendsen at 800 K / 0 bar for the model density, then Langevin NVT 800 K, then 15 ps VelocityVerlet NVE; D from the MSD slope, block-averaged uncertainty. On this shared GB10 GPU it ran at about 0.1-0.2 s/step even with 128 atoms in float32 (a first 250-atom float64 attempt was abandoned for the same reason). After ~20 min of CPU time the melt+NPT stages had not finished, so no NVE trajectory, energy drift or D exists. Only validation completed: MACE-MP-0 static bcc Li lattice constant a0 = 3.500 A. Not compared against a measured value here; it is not in tier1.json, which has no Li records. Measured reference to use for validation: Murday & Cotts, J. Chem. Phys. 48, 4938 (1968), NMR self-diffusion of liquid Li; its numbers were not retrieved, so none are quoted. To retry: use a batched GPU integrator (nvalchemi dynamics), or a less loaded GPU, at about 128-250 atoms, >=20 ps NVE, plus a Yeh-Hummer finite-size note. No value is reported.\"}' --parent 7dcf80a5-99cc-4ffc-99b5-c46019823833"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":477,"cache_read_input_tokens":37509,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":47