{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgbxVbfVQB8H6GfTrMrVW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I don't have a self-diffusion coefficient for liquid Li at 800 K: the simulation never reached the NVE production stage. I posted a `\"failed\"` run report to the board (`e6e16bff-2e4a-4734-a39f-4bcd8330a907`) under candidate `7dcf80a5…`, with no value.\n\n- **Premise check:** the task is well-posed. Li melts at 453.7 K, so 800 K is clearly liquid, and the coefficient can be measured from how far atoms wander over time in a few tens of picoseconds of constant-energy (NVE) MD.\n- **What I ran:** ASE with the MACE-MP-0 medium model and a 1 fs timestep. The protocol was: melt at 1500 K, a constant-pressure stage at 800 K to find the model's liquid density, a thermostatted stage at 800 K, then NVE (velocity Verlet) production while tracking energy drift.\n- **Why it failed:** the shared GPU was already 89% busy before I started, and the run managed only about 0.1–0.2 s per step.\n  - My first attempt (250 atoms, double precision) was too slow, so I killed it.\n  - The second (128 atoms, single precision) used about 20 minutes of CPU time without finishing the melt and constant-pressure stages.\n  - With the budget nearly spent, I stopped it rather than post an unvalidated number. No trajectory, energy-drift check or uncertainty exists.\n- **Validation done:** only one partial check. The model gives a bcc Li lattice constant of 3.500 Å at 0 K. I haven't compared it with a measured value; the calibration file has no Li records.\n- **Experimental reference:** the web search found Murday & Cotts, J. Chem. Phys. 48, 4938 (1968), which measured liquid-Li self-diffusion by NMR. I couldn't get its numbers, so I quoted none.\n\nTo retry, use a less loaded GPU or the toolkit's own batched GPU integrator instead of ASE's per-step loop. Run 128–250 atoms with at least 20 ps of NVE, and add a note on box-size (finite-size) effects. The script is at `/work/run/li.py`.\n\nSources:\n- [Self-diffusion coefficient study of liquid lithium (XJTU)](https://scholar.xjtu.edu.cn/en/publications/self-diffusion-coefficient-study-of-liquid-lithium/)\n- [Springer reference list citing Murday & Cotts 1968](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF00883553)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1007,"cache_read_input_tokens":37986,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1007,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":794,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9c452f78-34bc-4273-98ea-540346e2ed75","uuid":"530d728a-d3c9-4907-9fcd-08692afa9019","timestamp":"2026-11-01T09:17:56.992Z","request_id":"req_011CgbxVbGRXeVeV1ousTkjp"}
